{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/826350-lines-to-evoke-gaming-or-really-any-creative-concepts","id":826350,"title":"Lines to evoke gaming (or really any creative) concepts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-08T15:56:14-08:00","id":826350,"title":"Lines to evoke gaming (or really any creative) concepts","content":"I was recently reading randomly and came across a few different translations of &quot;I am become Death, destroyer of worlds&quot; one of which I really like, &quot;I am Time grown old to destroy the world, Embarked on the course of world annihilation&quot;.<br /> <br /> Are there any lines that you find inspire you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T16:27:47-08:00","id":826376,"title":"","content":"Everyone is the protagonist of their own story, even the villain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T19:28:38-08:00","id":826478,"title":"","content":"Men protect their children from the things that made themselves men. - Someone tell me where this is from.<br /> <br /> It is foolish and wrong to mourn the men who died. Rather we should thank God that such men lived. - General Patton<br /> <br /> Do not go gentle into that good night, Old age should burn and rave at close of day; Rage, rage against the dying of the light. - Dylan Thomas<br /> <br /> All gods who receive homage are cruel. All gods dispense suffering without reason. Otherwise they would not be worshipped. Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion. It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom. Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood. - Zora Neale Hurston<br /> <br /> The caged bird sings<br /> with a fearful trill<br /> of things unknown<br /> but longed for still<br /> and his tune is heard<br /> on the distant hill<br /> for the caged bird<br /> sings of freedom.<br /> - Caged Bird, by Maya Angelou<br /> <br /> Do not injustice to another<br /> Defend the weak and innocent<br /> Let truth and honor always guide you<br /> Let courage find a life within<br /> Stand up when no one else is willing<br /> Act not in hatred or in spite<br /> Be to this world as a perfect knight<br /> Even if it means your life<br /> - Sophia, by the Cruxshadows","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-08-2016, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T21:20:02-08:00","id":826535,"title":"","content":"When I reflect on my companions' inner natures I usually wish I controlled one small talent. I wish I could look inside them and unmask the darks and brights that move them. Then I take a quick look into the jungle of my own soul and thank heaven that I cannot. Any man who barely sustains an armistice with himself has no business poking around in an alien soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}